("M", "Which spies brought back a good report of the land along with Joshua?", "Caleb", ["Phinehas", "Shammua", "Igal"], "Numbers 13:30", "Caleb said the people should go up and possess the land.", "He later received Hebron as an inheritance."),
("M", "Which bird did God send to feed Elijah beside the brook Cherith?", "Ravens", ["Doves", "Eagles", "Sparrows"], "1 Kings 17:4–6", "God commanded ravens to bring bread and meat to Elijah.", "The brook is east of the Jordan."),
("M", "Who was the widow of Zarephath who fed Elijah?", "A widow", ["A queen", "A princess", "A servant girl"], "1 Kings 17:9–16", "The widow shared her last meal with the prophet and God kept her jar of meal full.", "She lived in Sidon."),
("M", "Which prophet was taken up by a whirlwind into heaven?", "Elijah", ["Elisha", "Enoch", "Moses"], "2 Kings 2:11", "Elijah was taken up while Elisha watched.", "A chariot of fire appeared."),
("M", "Which king of Israel was known for turning to the Lord with all his heart after Moses' law?", "Josiah", ["Jehoash", "Asa", "Joash"], "2 Kings 23:25", "No king before or after him turned to the Lord as he did.", "He reformed worship in the land."),
("M", "Which king of Israel was rebuked by the prophet Ahijah for splitting the nation?", "Jeroboam", ["Rehoboam", "Abijah", "Nadab"], "1 Kings 11:29–39", "Ahijah tore his garment and told Jeroboam he would rule ten tribes.", "He set up golden calves at Bethel and Dan."),
("M", "Who was the son of Solomon who lost the ten tribes?", "Rehoboam", ["Abijah", "Asa", "Jehoram"], "1 Kings 12:16–20", "Rehoboam refused the request of the people and most of the tribes rebelled.", "He listened to his young advisers."),
("M", "What were the names of the two golden calves set up by Jeroboam?", "Bethel and Dan", ["Shiloh and Gilgal", "Hebron and Beersheba", "Jericho and Ai"], "1 Kings 12:28–29", "Jeroboam set up calves at Bethel and Dan to keep the people from Jerusalem.", "Both towns are in the north."),
("M", "Which man saw the Lord sitting on a throne high and lifted up in the temple?", "Isaiah", ["Ezekiel", "Daniel", "Micah"], "Isaiah 6:1", "Isaiah saw the glory of the Lord in a vision.", "The seraphim cried 'Holy, holy, holy'."),
("M", "Which prophet was taken into Babylon with Ezekiel?", "Daniel", ["Jeremiah", "Obadiah", "Hosea"], "Daniel 1:6", "Daniel and his friends were taken to Babylon as young men.", "Their names were changed."),
("M", "What were the Hebrew names of Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego?", "Hananiah, Mishael and Azariah", ["Elnathan, Abihu and Mattaniah", "Eliab, Gershom and Amram", "Micah, Jonathan and Hosea"], "Daniel 1:6–7", "Their Babylonian names were given by the king's officer.", "Daniel's Hebrew name was Daniel too."),
("M", "Who was thrown into a fiery furnace and not harmed?", "Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego", ["Daniel and Hananiah", "Ezekiel and Jeremiah", "Moses and Aaron"], "Daniel 3:19–27", "God protected the three friends in the furnace.", "A fourth figure was seen with them."),
("M", "Which Babylonian king saw the writing on the wall?", "Belshazzar", ["Nebuchadnezzar", "Cyrus", "Darius"], "Daniel 5:5", "A hand wrote on the plaster of the palace wall at a feast.", "Daniel interpreted the writing."),
("M", "Which words did Daniel read on the wall: 'MENE, MENE, TEKEL, UPHARSIN'?", "Weighed, numbered, divided", ["Blessed, holy, lifted", "Peace, joy, honour", "Fire, flood, famine"], "Daniel 5:25–28", "Daniel explained that the kingdom had been weighed and found wanting.", "The words describe the kingdom's end."),
("M", "Which king of Persia allowed the Jews to return to Jerusalem?", "Cyrus", ["Darius", "Artaxerxes", "Xerxes"], "Ezra 1:1–3", "Cyrus made a decree that the temple should be rebuilt.", "He is called God's anointed in Isaiah."),
("M", "Which Persian king made Esther his queen?", "Xerxes", ["Cyrus", "Darius", "Artaxerxes"], "Esther 2:17", "Xerxes, also called Ahasuerus, chose Esther after Vashti was removed.", "Vashti refused to come when called."),
("M", "Who was Mordecai's cousin who was raised by him?", "Esther", ["Ruth", "Miriam", "Vashti"], "Esther 2:7", "Esther was an orphan and Mordecai raised her as his own daughter.", "She was of the tribe of Benjamin."),
("M", "What feast was established to remember the deliverance of the Jews in Esther's time?", "Purim", ["Passover", "Pentecost", "Tabernacles"], "Esther 9:26–28", "The feast of Purim was celebrated as a memorial of the deliverance.", "Lots were cast before Haman."),
("M", "Which wicked official plotted to destroy the Jews in Persia?", "Haman", ["Mordecai", "Nehemiah", "Sanballat"], "Esther 3:6", "Haman was angry that Mordecai would not bow down to him.", "He was hanged on the gallows he had built."),
("M", "Which prophet was sent to speak to Eli's family about their disobedience?", "A man of God", ["Nathan", "Gad", "Elkanah"], "1 Samuel 2:27", "An unnamed man of God pronounced judgement on Eli's house.", "The Bible does not give his name here."),
("M", "Which priest's sons, Hophni and Phinehas, were wicked?", "Eli", ["Samuel", "Zadok", "Abiathar"], "1 Samuel 2:12", "Eli's sons did not know the Lord and abused the offerings.", "They died in battle."),
("M", "What was the name of the ark's temporary home in the Philistine city of Ashdod?", "The temple of Dagon", ["The house of Obed-edom", "The temple of Baal", "The house of Abinadab"], "1 Samuel 5:2", "The Philistines placed the ark beside their god Dagon, which fell down.", "Dagon was a Philistine god."),
("M", "Who was the first king of the northern kingdom after the division?", "Jeroboam", ["Rehoboam", "Omri", "Jehu"], "1 Kings 12:20", "Jeroboam was made king over Israel after the ten tribes rebelled.", "He set up golden calves."),
("M", "What is the name of the valley where Gideon's men drank water?", "The valley of Jezreel", ["The valley of Hinnom", "The valley of Sorek", "The valley of Elah"], "Judges 6:33", "The Midianites gathered in the valley of Jezreel.", "Gideon's army camped near the spring of Harod."),
("M", "Which judge sacrificed his daughter because of a vow?", "Jephthah", ["Gideon", "Ehud", "Abdon"], "Judges 11:30–31", "Jephthah made a vow before battle and his daughter came out to meet him.", "He was a Gileadite."),
("M", "Which of the sons of Jacob was a judge of Israel?", "There is no one of Jacob's sons who was a judge", ["Judah", "Levi", "Dan"], "Judges 10:1", "This is a trick: the judges listed were from other tribes.", "Choose the option the story does not mention."),
("M", "Who was the Edomite king who was not an Israelite but ruled before Israel had a king?", "Bela", ["Saul", "Eglon", "Ehud"], "Genesis 36:31–32", "Genesis lists the kings of Edom before Israel had a king.", "He was the son of Beor."),
("M", "Which king of Moab was defeated by Ehud?", "Eglon", ["Balak", "Sihon", "Og"], "Judges 3:20–21", "Ehud killed Eglon with a dagger in his private chamber.", "He was left-handed."),
("M", "Which king of Bashan had a bed of iron?", "Og", ["Sihon", "Balak", "Eglon"], "Deuteronomy 3:11", "Og was a giant king of Bashan who was defeated by Israel.", "His bed was nine cubits long."),
("M", "Which king of the Amorites refused Israel passage through his land?", "Sihon", ["Og", "Balak", "Eglon"], "Numbers 21:23", "Sihon gathered his army and fought against Israel.", "Israel took his land east of the Jordan."),
("M", "Who was the Moabite king who hired Balaam to curse Israel?", "Balak", ["Sihon", "Eglon", "Og"], "Numbers 22:2–6", "Balak sent messengers to Balaam to curse the people.", "He was afraid of Israel's numbers."),
("M", "What was the name of the man from Midian who married a Moabite woman and was killed by Phinehas?", "Zimri", ["Korah", "Dathan", "Abiram"], "Numbers 25:14", "Zimri brought a Midianite woman into the camp in public.", "Phinehas stopped the plague by his zeal."),
("M", "Which man was Moses' father-in-law who advised him to appoint judges?", "Jethro", ["Hobab", "Reuel", "Laban"], "Exodus 18:17–21", "Jethro suggested sharing the burden of judging the people.", "He was a priest of Midian."),
("M", "Who was Moses' wife who was a Midianite?", "Zipporah", ["Miriam", "Rahab", "Hagar"], "Exodus 2:21", "Zipporah was the daughter of Reuel, a priest of Midian.", "She circumcised their son."),
("M", "Which prophet raised the son of the Shunammite woman from the dead?", "Elisha", ["Elijah", "Samuel", "Ezekiel"], "2 Kings 4:34–35", "Elisha lay on the child and his flesh became warm.", "He was the servant of Elijah."),
("M", "Which prophet was known as the 'man of God' who prophesied to Jeroboam at Bethel?", "A man of God from Judah", ["Shemaiah", "Iddo", "Azariah"], "1 Kings 13:1–2", "The prophet from Judah spoke against the altar at Bethel.", "The Bible describes him as coming from Judah."),
("M", "Which king had a wife named Athaliah who killed the royal family?", "Ahaziah", ["Joram", "Jehoash", "Ahab"], "2 Kings 11:1", "Athaliah destroyed the royal family, but Joash was hidden in the temple.", "She was the daughter of Ahab."),
("M", "Which priest hid the young king Joash in the temple?", "Jehoiada", ["Hilkiah", "Eli", "Zadok"], "2 Kings 11:2–3", "Jehoiada rescued Joash and later helped him become king.", "He was the high priest."),
("M", "Which prophet told King Asa he would be strong if he trusted God?", "Azariah", ["Obed", "Iddo", "Hanani"], "2 Chronicles 15:1–2", "Azariah reminded Asa that the Lord is with those who are with him.", "Asa had won against a great army."),
("M", "Who was the Moabite woman who said 'Whither thou goest, I will go'?", "Ruth", ["Orpah", "Naomi", "Rahab"], "Ruth 1:16", "Ruth committed herself to Naomi and her people.", "Orpah returned to her family."),
("M", "Which man sat under a tree while God revealed he would be the deliverer of Israel?", "Gideon", ["Barak", "Samson", "Ehud"], "Judges 6:11", "The angel of the Lord sat under an oak tree in Ophrah.", "He was threshing wheat in a winepress."),
("M", "Which warrior judge was helped by Deborah?", "Barak", ["Gideon", "Jephthah", "Othniel"], "Judges 4:6–8", "Barak agreed to fight only if Deborah went with him.", "He was from Naphtali."),
("M", "Which woman was given a son after her prayers, and then sang a song of thanksgiving?", "Hannah", ["Miriam", "Deborah", "Rebekah"], "1 Samuel 2:1", "Hannah praised God for his salvation and for lifting up the poor.", "Her son was Samuel."),
("M", "Who said 'Speak, LORD; for thy servant heareth'?", "Samuel", ["Eli", "Nathan", "Gad"], "1 Samuel 3:9–10", "The boy Samuel answered God's call in the temple.", "He grew up in the house of Eli."),
("M", "Which king of Israel's son was the one who sat at the king's table with lame feet?", "Mephibosheth", ["Ishbosheth", "Adonijah", "Absalom"], "2 Samuel 9:13", "David showed kindness to Jonathan's son by inviting him to eat at the king's table.", "He was crippled in both feet as a child."),
("M", "Who was the commander of David's army who killed Uriah?", "Joab", ["Abner", "Amasa", "Benaiah"], "2 Samuel 11:14–17", "Joab arranged for Uriah to be placed in danger in battle.", "He was David's nephew."),
("M", "Which man was David's son who killed Amnon?", "Absalom", ["Adonijah", "Shammah", "Chileab"], "2 Samuel 13:28–29", "Absalom had Amnon killed after the attack on Tamar.", "He later rebelled against David."),
("M", "Which king had a counsellor named Ahithophel who joined Absalom's rebellion?", "David", ["Saul", "Solomon", "Hezekiah"], "2 Samuel 15:12", "Ahithophel supported Absalom against his former king.", "The king fled Jerusalem."),
("M", "Who cursed David as he fled from Absalom?", "Shimei", ["Joab", "Abishai", "Ittai"], "2 Samuel 16:5–6", "Shimei threw stones and cursed the king on the road.", "He was from the family of Saul."),
("M", "Which captain of David's army was Absalom's cousin and fought against him?", "Joab", ["Abishai", "Benaiah", "Ittai"], "2 Samuel 18:14", "Joab killed Absalom when his hair caught in an oak tree.", "He was the commander of the army."),
